.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::SplitBoundary\fP< dim >::PullApartSplitBoundary (double dist)"

.PP
Method that applies half of displacement to both sides of interface (dotted by unitNormal) Iterates of \fBInterFace\fP objects and displaces nodes by param dist/2 on both sides, opening up the interface\&. Leaves middle nodes untouched\&. Uses InterFace->UnitNormal() from bisector plane or middle element

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdist\fP is the final aperture the nodes will have\&. Each side is displaced by dist/2\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::SplitBoundary\fP< dim >::SurfaceIntegral (const \fBPropertyDatabase\fP< dim > & p, const char * property, \fBINTERFACE_SIDE\fP side = \fRINSIDE\fP) const"

.PP
integrates the property over the boundary line or surface Integrates a scalar variable of interest over the target side of the \fBSplitBoundary\fP using the current finite element basis functions\&. Dependent on the placement of the variable it is either read from the \fBInterFace\fP or the target sidfe of the boundary\&. Potential incompatibilities are checked\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
for simplex element node and integration point properties are integrated using their value projected to the element barycentre\&.
.RE
.PP
If the variable is vector quantity, it is projected onto the outward pointing normals of the boundary \fBInterFace\fP objects, multiplying the boundary normal componet with their area\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 21/8/2018 
.RE
.PP

